2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Regression\040Estimator\040for\040the\040Tail\040Index)
/Author (László\040Németh\054\040András\040Zempléni)
/Subject (Estimating\040the\040tail\040index\040parameter\040is\040one\040of\040the\040primal\040objectives\040in\040extreme\040value\040theory\040For\040heavy\055tailed\040distributions\040the\040Hill\040estimator\040is\040the\040most\040popular\040way\040to\040estimate\040this\040parameter\040Several\040recent\040publications\220\040aim\040was\040to\040improve\040the\040Hill\040estimator\054\040using\040different\040methods\054\040for\040example\040the\040bootstrap\054\040or\040the\040Kolmogorov\205Smirnov\040metric\040These\040methods\040are\040asymptotically\040consistent\054\040but\040for\040tail\040index\040\044\044\134xi\040\07605\044\044\012\040the\040estimations\040fail\040to\040approach\040the\040theoretical\040value\040for\040realistic\040sample\040sizes\040In\040this\040paper\054\040we\040introduce\040new\040empirical\040methods\054\040which\040combine\040the\040advantages\040of\040the\040Kolmogorov\205Smirnov\040approach\040and\040the\040bootstrap\040We\040demonstrate\040that\040our\040estimators\040are\040able\040to\040estimate\040large\040tail\040index\040parameters\040well\040and\040might\040also\040be\040useful\040for\040relatively\040small\040sample\040sizes\040As\040an\040application\054\040we\040consider\040the\040classic\040Danish\040fire\040data\040set\040and\040the\040most\040destructive\040natural\040disasters\040in\040Europe)
/Keywords (01\040Sep\0402020\054\040Journal\040of\040statistical\040theory\040and\040practice\054\040Estimator\054\040Extreme\040value\040theory\054\040Sample\040size\040determination\054\040Eötvös\040Loránd\040University)
>>
endobj
